WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.990 align:start position:0%
 
outriders is a game that isn't defined  by big new ideas  but a variety of familiar elements mixed  together in experimental ways  it's a role-playing game with loot  shooter elements it's a serious dark  sci-fi story with a big dose of  goofiness and humor  it's a cover shooter that demands you  rush out and smash enemies with  ludicrous superpowers  whether this mixture works for you will  determine how much you'll enjoy it  [Music]  though outriders looks like a loot  shooter live game  it's actually much more mass effect 3  than destiny 2.  like in mass effect rpg progression and  cover shooting are much more important  than chasing the next new gun  outriders is a cover shooter rpg with a  hearty dose of gear progression  leaning heavily into an epic story told  with tons of dialogue cut scenes and  collectible lore  developer people can fly draws a lot  from its past work on the gears of war  series  rifle-toting enemies take fortified  positions to unload on you at a distance  backed up by shotgunners that try to  close the gap armored troops with chain  guns plotting in the open  and cleaver wielding sprinters who  charge straight at your face to drive  you out of cover  the core of outriders is shooting and  you'll have a mess of guns at your  disposal  though you can only have two main  weapons and a sidearm equipped at any  given time  you'll have lots of options thanks to  the loot shooter half of the outrider's  formula  that means you can pair a sniper rifle  with a shotgun or assault rifles with  smgs  and since you're constantly searching  for weapons with better stats  you'll cycle through a lot of different  loadouts in a short amount of time  what makes these guns especially fun are  the myriad different properties and  status effects they can have  like dispensing poison blowing enemies  up freezing people solid  and so on recalling gears of war again a  writer shooting reliably feels good  but finding synergies between your  weapon's weird properties  is a lot of what makes the shooting part  of the game rewarding  things get a bit weirder as outriders  merges space superpowers with its cover  shooter core  you could choose from one of four  character classes early in the game  devastator trickster pyromancer or  technomancer  these each have the general roles of  tank rogue  damage focused mage and debuff focused  mage the devastator uses gravity attacks  for close range kills  the trickster teleports around to get  the drop on enemies  the pyromancer is a mid-range fire  flinger and the technomancer can summon  turrets and rockets  that also poison or slow targets each  class has a different way of  replenishing health through combat  generally by focusing on their specific  strengths the devastator for instance  heals you for every close range kill  encouraging you to get in close to  enemies to hit them with powers like a  small earthquake  combat becomes a constant calculus  between when to cut the distance and  take down an enemy  and when to take cover bide your time  and protect yourself  that combination can be a bit confusing  and as a result  combat is a place where outriders can  both sprint and stumble  you're playing a shooter where you use  cover to keep yourself alive  but you're encouraged to leave cover to  keep yourself alive  that push and pull of avoiding incoming  damage and taking the fight to the enemy  means that you constantly have to be  managing the battlefield  as well as your ability cooldown timers  if you jump out of cover and go wild  with all your powers on an approaching  enemy  you leave yourself exposed for all their  friends and quickly find yourself cut  down by incoming fire  that means that having an earthquake  ready to stun incoming fighters is  essential to saving your life  since it allows you to grab kills while  keeping your head down  similarly abilities like the trickster's  teleport which instantly puts you behind  enemies who are in cover  are just as useful for dramatically  repositioning yourself across the  battlefield  as they are for eliminating foes but you  can rarely just go  all out with your guns and abilities you  really have to think about where you are  where your enemies are and how you can  best eliminate them without exposing  yourself  it can feel unintuitive for a while but  when you do find the balance between  using your powers  healing yourself and staying out of fire  outriders can create some pitched  frantic battles that use cover just  enough to give you a second to breathe  without nailing your shoulder to a  single chest high wall  and leaving you there for minutes on end  but there are also times when you'll  find yourself surrounded or cut off  trapped between enemies unable to kill  anything fast enough  or escape the onslaught to save yourself  sometimes a situation will just feel  unwinnable  but luckily outriders generally sets you  back only a bit when you die  so you can re-enter a fight quickly and  try a new approach  facing tougher altered enemies who have  power similar to yours  can result in battles of attrition where  you have to cheese the situation  by scurrying out of the arena so enemies  don't all chase you down at once  sometimes even careful management of  powers cover and your spacing on the  battlefield  aren't enough to save you and it's these  moments when outriders can get  frustrating  because it doesn't feel like you're  losing for lack of skill there are ways  to deal with that issue  outriders is largely pretty open and has  liberal fast travel  so you can bail on a mission and go do  side quests to grab rewards that can  boost your gear and character  the difficulty of enemies is also  determined by your overall  world tier level which rises as you earn  experience points alongside your  character level  world tier also determines loot drops so  there is an incentive to keep it on the  highest level you can  but if you're in a particularly annoying  fight you could always back it down a  touch to keep yourself from stalling  the world tier is a smart solution to  the difficulty problem  and since it can be adjusted anytime it  gives you a lot of freedom to avoid  frustration  at key moments i'm only about 10 or so  hours into outriders  so it's difficult to say how all its  elements gel over the long term  so far though i'm intrigued by the way  it blends disparate ideas together to  create new flavors  while the combat can be tough to wrap  your head around it first the frenetic  balancing  act has created some heart-pounding  moments more fun  and intense battles than annoying ones  you can also play almost all about  riders cooperatively  which seems like it could go a long way  toward lessening combat irritations  and while i haven't had a chance to team  up with anyone else yet i can already  see how powers  abilities and gear might work together  on teams  to create fun synergies outrider's story  also has me pretty hooked in  people can fly has obviously put a lot  of time and thought into the game's lore  and there's a lot of interesting writing  to be found in journal entries and side  quests  what i'm liking most though is the  unexpected mixture of desperation  and humor the planet enoch is a war-torn  hellscape where the last vestiges of the  human race  are literally ripping each other apart  the misery and torment of the situation  is made worse by the altered  like your character who basically have  gained godlike power  how those people choose to use that  power is an ongoing moral question  and i'm interested in the way the game  is attempting to explore it  coupled with the dark serious and gritty  sci-fi take though  are the moments of levity that make  outriders characters feel human  side missions in particular have you  interacting with weird characters  like a drug-addled military commander or  a vinyl loving collector of earth  artifact  and your character's attitude is almost  always one of vague but funny annoyance  at doing their small scale favors  come on get out of there you out of your  mind  i'm leaving this your [ __ ] out until the  sun's all the way up  i'm not waiting around here for the sun  to come out there are a lot of these  moments where outrider strikes a  delicate balance between  being serious and being light developing  its world and recognizing that it's  dealing in some  fairly absurd concepts these moments  likely won't land for everyone  it can feel a touch edge lord at times  although rarely so far  and the tone can ping-pong between  extremes especially jumping off the main  quest to explore side content but those  swings are also where  outriders excels if you meet it where it  is its story is often funny but  similarly intense its combat requires  you to take cover and to charge  its abilities make you phenomenally  powerful but prone to overestimating  yourself  if you can find the balance in outriders  the rpg shooter finds ways to combine  well-worn video game ideas  into something new and fun whether those  new combinations will carry it all the  way through its seemingly expansive run  time  remains to be seen but i'm excited to  see what still waits in the wilds of  enoch  and to smash it with seismic earthquake  magic  [Music]  foreign

